# Personal data and credentials. The committed configuration under
# backend/src/main/resources/leadgen/ names its values as ${PLACEHOLDERS}; the
# values themselves live here and are never committed.
#
# `.env.*` as well, because a hand-made copy — .env.bak, .env.local, .env.old — carries
# the same keys as the original and is exactly what gets committed by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that matters: an unanchored `config/`
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed every
# new file under backend/src/main/java/.../config/ and .../test/.../config/.
# Already-tracked files stayed tracked, so nothing looked wrong — only new ones
# vanished from `git status`.
/config/
# These two stay unanchored on purpose: they are output directories, and the
# working directory differs by how the service was started — `bootRun` runs in
# backend/, a jar wherever it sits. An anchored pattern would miss
# backend/packages/ the first time someone runs the digest from Gradle.
packages/
data/
*.log

# Real newsletter mails and anything derived from them: they carry the
# subscriber's mail address in headers and unsubscribe links.
docs/samples/emails/
# The search-agent mails from the two portals, same reason: they name the subscriber in
# the body and carry the address as a mailto in the footer.
docs/samples/emails-freelance-de/
docs/samples/emails-freelancermap/
docs/samples/extracted.json
# What the reference measured, written by simulate_filter.py. Derived from the corpus and
# from config/, so it is gitignored with them.
docs/samples/filter-baseline.json
# The working list exported for measure_embeddings.ts, and what it wrote: both name real
# adverts, so they are corpus-derived like everything above. A pattern and not the one name,
# because the script takes `--offers=NAME` and a second export carries the same adverts.
docs/samples/offers*.json
docs/samples/embedding-observed-*.md
# Which of your projects a letter would pitch, per advert: names real adverts and reads the
# individual profile, so it is corpus-derived like everything above.
docs/samples/reference-selection-*.md
docs/samples/embedding-cache-*.json
# The analysis scripts are the reference implementation and stay in the repo:
!docs/samples/analyze_samples.py
!docs/samples/simulate_filter.py
!docs/samples/measure_embeddings.ts
!docs/samples/measure_references.ts

# Build
target/
build/
node_modules/
dist/
.gradle/
.angular/
frontend/.angular/
frontend/dist/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# Agent scratch state — carries absolute paths from whoever's machine wrote it.
.checkpoint-state.json

# OS & IDE
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.iml

# Claude & AI
Plans
MEMORY

# Python bytecode from running the reference scripts in docs/samples/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The Ideal State Artifact is a working document, not project documentation.
ISA.md

# Coverage reports. Produced by `./gradlew check`, never committed.
/coverage/
frontend/coverage/

# The demo uses the repository as its configuration directory, so its manual inbox
# is a working directory rather than a committed one.
demo/inbox/
